# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
aquinas-first-way.md:1: argue/readings: S11 is read 2 ways: aquinas-first-way.logic.r3 and aquinas-first-way.logic.r3.2 have "moved_by_another → infinite_regress ∨ first_mover"; aquinas-first-way.logic.r3.3 has nothing from it; they differ when only "whatever is in motion is put in motion by another" is true, which the second allows
aquinas-first-way.md:1: argue/answered: S11: answered yes, which keeps aquinas-first-way.logic.r3.3, to: Suppose "whatever is in motion is put in motion by another" is true and "the series of movers put in motion by another goes on to infinity" and "there is a first mover, put in motion by no other" are false. Is S11, "If that by which it is put in motion be itself put in motion, then this also must needs be put in motion by another, and that by another again.", true then?
aquinas-first-way.logic.r3: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 3 ways: aquinas-first-way.logic.r3 has "moved_potential ∧ mover_actual ∧ motion_is_actualization ∧ actualization_needs_actual → □(self_motion → same_act_pot)" and "self_motion ∨ moved_by_another" and "some_motion → other_movers"; aquinas-first-way.logic.r3.2 has "moved_potential ∧ mover_actual → □(self_motion → same_act_pot)" and "motion_is_actualization ∧ actualization_needs_actual ∧ ¬◇self_motion → moved_by_another" and "some_motion ∧ moved_by_another → other_movers"; they differ when only "in the world some things are in motion", "whatever is in motion is in potentiality to that towards which it is in motion", "a thing moves inasmuch as it is in act", "motion is nothing else than the reduction of something from potentiality to actuality", "a thing is both mover and moved in the same respect, i.e. moves itself", "whatever is in motion is put in motion by another" and "there are subsequent (other) movers" are true, which the first allows; aquinas-first-way.logic.r3.3 has "moved_potential ∧ mover_actual → □(self_motion → same_act_pot)" and "motion_is_actualization ∧ actualization_needs_actual ∧ ¬◇self_motion → moved_by_another" and "some_motion ∧ moved_by_another → other_movers" and "moved_by_another ∧ ¬infinite_regress → first_mover"
